# TB1: TIMED arm B (first of two) of the paired timing ABAB on coding prompts (audits OFF). Arms alternate A B A B in this one image, each after its own all-four reset, same admission order:
# A = c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace (the control: production's recipe as a gate-only twin, the pinned sampler in the verify trace), B = c2-packed-tp4-speed-warm4 (no sampler in the trace, the request-width warm on).
# Expected B - A about -4.4 ms per round (sampler argmax/glue -2.9 and the sampler collective -1.5, about 3%). Judge each pair PAIRED per round, never by unpaired medians: read the [PACKED-PHASE] verify
# trace_ms and the round wall at 4 live; check the load average around each run. Then offline: python scripts/ci/speed_window_compare.py <A results> <B results> --users 0,1,2,3 --position-keyed
# --strict-concurrent-prefixes (expect exit 0: nothing in the drafter changes; B's served text must equal A's in both pairs). B not at least 2 ms per round faster in both pairs is 'no gain'.
# A hang or different text on a B arm stops the timing and blocks promotion. Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min, build 10-20 min, tests 15-35 min: 30-60 min.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/warm4 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/warm4 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or
# a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-warm4a is a PLACEHOLDER for ONE FRESH tag, built by B0 from the pushed tp4/warm4 commit; the driver
# substitutes it in every template once the image is built. A later commit needs a new tag.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-warm4a
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-warm4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4_code_equal,concurrent4_code_32k
